  "raw_response": "```python\ndef solve(grid):\n    if not grid:\n        return []\n    n = len(grid)\n    m = len(grid[0])\n    \n    # Identify non-zero colors\n    colors = set()\n    for row in grid:\n        for val in row:\n            if val != 0:\n                colors.add(val)\n    colors = list(colors)\n    \n    if len(colors) == 0:\n        return [[]]\n    \n    best_area = -1\n    best_rect = None\n    frame_color = None\n    \n    # Search for the largest rectangular frame\n    for C in colors:\n        for r1 in range(n):\n            for c1 in range(m):\n                if grid[r1][c1] != C:\n                    continue\n                for r2 in range(r1 + 2, n):\n                    if grid[r2][c1] != C:\n                        break\n                    for c2 in range(c1 + 2, m):\n                        if grid[r1][c2] != C or grid[r2][c2] != C:\n                            continue\n                        # Check top border\n                        valid = True\n                        for c in range(c1, c2 + 1):\n                            if grid[r1][c] != C:\n                                valid = False\n                                break\n                        if not valid:\n                            continue\n                        # Check bottom border\n                        for c in range(c1, c2 + 1):\n                            if grid[r2][c] != C:\n                                valid = False\n                                break\n                        if not valid:\n                            continue\n                        # Check left border\n                        for r in range(r1, r2 + 1):\n                            if grid[r][c1] != C:\n                                valid = False\n                                break\n                        if not valid:\n                            break\n                        # Check right border\n                        for r in range(r1, r2 + 1):\n                            if grid[r][c2] != C:\n                                valid = False\n                                break\n                        if not valid:\n                            continue\n                        # Valid rectangle found\n                        area = (r2 - r1 + 1) * (c2 - c1 + 1)\n                        if area > best_area:\n                            best_area = area\n                            best_rect = (r1, c1, r2, c2)\n                            frame_color = C\n    \n    if best_rect is None:\n        return [[]]\n    \n    r1, c1, r2, c2 = best_rect\n    h = r2 - r1 + 1\n    w = c2 - c1 + 1\n    \n    # The marker color is the other non-zero color\n    if len(colors) == 1:\n        marker = colors[0]\n    else:\n        marker = [c for c in colors if c != frame_color][0]\n    \n    # Construct output\n    out = [[0 for _ in range(w)] for _ in range(h)]\n    for i in range(h):\n        for j in range(w):\n            if i == 0 or i == h - 1 or j == 0 or j == w - 1:\n                out[i][j] = marker\n            else:\n                orig_val = grid[r1 + i][c1 + j]\n                out[i][j] = marker if orig_val == marker else 0\n    return out\n```",
  "script": "def solve(grid):\n    if not grid:\n        return []\n    n = len(grid)\n    m = len(grid[0])\n    \n    # Identify non-zero colors\n    colors = set()\n    for row in grid:\n        for val in row:\n            if val != 0:\n                colors.add(val)\n    colors = list(colors)\n    \n    if len(colors) == 0:\n        return [[]]\n    \n    best_area = -1\n    best_rect = None\n    frame_color = None\n    \n    # Search for the largest rectangular frame\n    for C in colors:\n        for r1 in range(n):\n            for c1 in range(m):\n                if grid[r1][c1] != C:\n                    continue\n                for r2 in range(r1 + 2, n):\n                    if grid[r2][c1] != C:\n                        break\n                    for c2 in range(c1 + 2, m):\n                        if grid[r1][c2] != C or grid[r2][c2] != C:\n                            continue\n                        # Check top border\n                        valid = True\n                        for c in range(c1, c2 + 1):\n                            if grid[r1][c] != C:\n                                valid = False\n                                break\n                        if not valid:\n                            continue\n                        # Check bottom border\n                        for c in range(c1, c2 + 1):\n                            if grid[r2][c] != C:\n                                valid = False\n                                break\n                        if not valid:\n                            continue\n                        # Check left border\n                        for r in range(r1, r2 + 1):\n                            if grid[r][c1] != C:\n                                valid = False\n                                break\n                        if not valid:\n                            break\n                        # Check right border\n                        for r in range(r1, r2 + 1):\n                            if grid[r][c2] != C:\n                                valid = False\n                                break\n                        if not valid:\n                            continue\n                        # Valid rectangle found\n                        area = (r2 - r1 + 1) * (c2 - c1 + 1)\n                        if area > best_area:\n                            best_area = area\n                            best_rect = (r1, c1, r2, c2)\n                            frame_color = C\n    \n    if best_rect is None:\n        return [[]]\n    \n    r1, c1, r2, c2 = best_rect\n    h = r2 - r1 + 1\n    w = c2 - c1 + 1\n    \n    # The marker color is the other non-zero color\n    if len(colors) == 1:\n        marker = colors[0]\n    else:\n        marker = [c for c in colors if c != frame_color][0]\n    \n    # Construct output\n    out = [[0 for _ in range(w)] for _ in range(h)]\n    for i in range(h):\n        for j in range(w):\n            if i == 0 or i == h - 1 or j == 0 or j == w - 1:\n                out[i][j] = marker\n            else:\n                orig_val = grid[r1 + i][c1 + j]\n                out[i][j] = marker if orig_val == marker else 0\n    return out",
